bump this file to build the Mac test zip (.github/workflows/arpezator-mac.yml): ArpEZator alone, VST3 + AU + app, a workflow artifact, no public release
build 3: ArpEZator 3.2.4 - a TEMPO switch under the SEED: 1/2x | 1x | 2x, each showing the BPM it plays at (65 / 130 / 260 when FL is at 130). It stays locked to FL's bars (2x = two of its bars in every FL bar); DRAG MIDI lands in FL exactly as you hear it (written at FL's tempo), DRAG AUDIO is rendered as you hear it with the BPM in the file name; saved with the project, a new ArpEZator starts at 1x.
build 2: ArpEZator 3.2.3 - opens at 1149 x 760, a size that fits FL Studio's plug-in window on a 1440 x 900 MacBook Pro (the picture's own proportions; still resizable; always this size when it opens), and a new ArpEZator is always a fresh start: HOOK LAB's learned taste is no longer shared between instances through a file (it learns within the instance). Tested: two at once, the second stays at factory defaults, and a new one plays its first idea. Built and installed on Brandon's own Mac.
build 1: ArpEZator 3.2.0 - MUTANT ARP: the melodic sequence generator (RAGE / ALIEN / DIGITAL / DREAM / HYPER / FLUTE), chord-aware cells with octave jumps, pedals and pings, neighbour and chromatic approach notes, ratchets and 1/64 bursts, a variation every 2 / 4 bars, LOCK NOTES, MUTATE / OCTAVE CHAOS / RHYTHM CHAOS, EVOLVE 4 / 8 / 16, TWO LINES (ANSWER / INTERLOCK / SHADOW into the MELODY lane), 1/4..1/64, reverse / ping-pong / rotate, swing, glide, DRAG MIDI; older sessions and every old mood untouched
build 2: the MUTANT ARP button's tooltip names all six modes (FLUTE was missing); TWO_ANSWER and TWO_SHADOW demos; no engine change
build 3: ArpEZator 3.2.1 - the TRAP flute sings: DARK / TRIUMPHANT / HYPNOTIC / DRILL write slow trap-flute melodies measured from the flute reference (short phrases of 1/8s and 1/4s ending on long held notes with vibrato, breaths, mostly stepwise with one leap, repeated-note stabs, grace notes that scoop in, trills, slides; a 2-bar call that ends open and a 2-bar answer that lands; HYPNOTIC loops one bar); versioned per idea (melVer) so every session saved before 3.2.1 renders exactly as it did, GENERATE / a NEW melody take move it to the new writer. MUTANT ARP: FLUTE's button becomes CYBERPOP, a mode that generates from a style table learned from MIDI packs by tools/learn_pack.py (aggregate statistics only: onset grid, note lengths, interval histogram, accents, ratchets, repeat form; no phrases, no names); until the first pack is learned the table is a seed. FLUTE stays hidden for older sessions (bit-identical, fingerprint test). Old moods / TRAP / HIP HOP / Ghost Slice old sessions bit-identical; OLD MOODS constants re-baselined against pre-branch main.
build 4: ArpEZator 3.2.2 - CYBERPOP learned from the first MIDI pack set (3 lead tracks, 195 notes; aggregate statistics only): 8th-grid hooks at ~5 notes a bar in a one-octave band, the second bar answering the first; the register and MUTATE come from the table, CHORD FOLLOW keeps a hook's pitches over the chord loop (nudges beats onto the chord), the pitch walk has its own random stream; the no-copy check: 0 shared 4-note sequences with any lead track over 480 generated files. FLUTE (hidden) bit-identical; old moods, TRAP / HIP HOP and Ghost Slice old sessions untouched.
build 5: ArpEZator 3.2.2 - CYBERPOP retune: the learned table now includes the chord pad's top line (4 melodic tracks, 202 notes; drums / 808s left out); the move draw is smoothed with a generic prior and comes from the pitch walk's own stream (NOTE DENSITY no longer re-rolls the tune); a zigzag stair (the stock 4-note pop-hook figure) is broken on its 4th note; no-copy check over 1,920 files: 0 shared 5-note sequences with any melodic track, 4-note lead coincidences 4 in 1,200 CYBERPOP lines (generic 3-move shapes). FLUTE (hidden), old moods, saved sessions (the cell is stored) and Ghost Slice untouched.
build 6: ArpEZator 3.2.5 - FACES: the look button is now a FACE list. BLACK / PURPLE / LIGHT / GHOST as before, plus four picture faces: HOLO (the rainy bus-stop city; every lane in the holographic raincoat's lilac / mint / pink with foil edges), NEON RAIN (the neon sign canyon in SUNRISE / DUSK / MIDNIGHT, the wet street with the tail lights in TRAP / HIP HOP; neon-tube edges, glowing title), MASK (the red / mustard / teal stencil face, its eyes looking through the piano roll; print-misregistration edges), DREAM (an original watercolour dawn on cream paper; pencil + wash edges), and AUTO (a face per mood: SUNRISE dream, DUSK holo, MIDNIGHT + TRAP neon rain, HIP HOP mask). Cards and the roll are frosted over the picture (pre-blurred copies, no run-time blur), saved with the project; older versions open a FACE project as BLACK.
build 7: ArpEZator 3.2.5 - FACES, part 2: the names in neon type per face (NEON RAIN: TILT NEON pink tubes; HOLO: AUDIOWIDE in raincoat foil; MASK: STARDOS STENCIL mustard on a red glow, teal plate; DREAM: MONOTON blush on teal; all OFL, licences beside the fonts), the professor logo re-lit per face (NEON: his outlines as pink -> cyan tubes; HOLO: foil; MASK: posterised stencil; DREAM: pastel + pencil), and the mood ghost redrawn anime-neon (neon rim, big shiny eyes in the mood's colour, hatched blush, twinkles; MASK: he wears the zip mask).
build 8: ArpEZator 3.2.5 - FACES, part 3: KITSUNE (an original red neon shrine-lantern stairway with ice-white fox masks; the TRAP face in AUTO; the mood ghost wears a little fox mask), NEON RAIN's sign canyon now mirrored in a rain puddle, and the professor logo redrawn as a clean neon sign per face (posts, hammock, the professor with his flask, rising bubbles) instead of re-lit pixels.
build 9: ArpEZator 3.2.5 - the professor's neon sign in full detail: brick backing, double frame tube with screws, capped posts, a diamond rope net, lab coat + lapels + bow tie, crossed legs and shoes, wild hair, brows, round glasses with eyes, curly moustache, the flask with its liquid, bubbles + steam, drifting music notes, twinkling stars and a moon tube that flickers now and then (the still part is cached once per face).
build 10: ArpEZator 3.2.5 - the logos redrawn per face AND per mood: the professor's neon sign keeps his original scenes (SUNRISE sunglasses + sun, DUSK the setting sun, MIDNIGHT stars + glowing glasses, TRAP the double foam cup, HIP HOP the bottle in the bag; round fluffy hair, round glasses) in each face's style, and the anime-neon mood ghost per face (MASK zip mask, KITSUNE fox mask, DREAM ink + wash).
build 11: ArpEZator 3.2.5 - the MUTANT ARP button only shows on the ARP lane (hidden on CHORDS / MELODY / BASS; switching away from ARP closes the MUTANT panel).
build 12: ArpEZator 3.2.5 - no more first-run 1 / 2 / 3 "click anywhere to start" hints when ArpEZator opens; it opens straight to the plugin.
build 13: ArpEZator 3.2.6 - the old BLACK / PURPLE / LIGHT / GHOST looks are gone: the FACE list is AUTO (the default: MIDNIGHT neon rain, DUSK holo, SUNRISE dream, TRAP kitsune, HIP HOP mask) or any one face, changeable any time; the ArpEZator name is much bigger on every face; CYCLE / RANGE no longer sits on OCT +; the lane hint stops before MUTANT ARP instead of running under it.
build 14: ArpEZator 3.2.7 - a new ArpEZator (and every mood you pick: SUNRISE / DUSK / MIDNIGHT / TRAP / HIP HOP) opens with CHORDS + MELODY + BASS playing and ARP muted (one click on its speaker brings it back); it opens on the CHORDS lane.
build 15: ArpEZator 3.2.8 - clicks gone: PUMP's dip on every beat now glides in (it dropped in one sample: a click on every beat on every lane), tied / legato notes (TRAP FLUTE etc.) glide up instead of jumping; DUSTY KEYS has no vinyl noise bed (it read as crackle); STUTTER on a drawn or HOOK LAB melody keeps your notes and only adds repeats (turn it down = your melody back) instead of writing a new melody; CLASSIC ARP's locked notes come back when MUTANT ARP goes off (MUTANT's locked steps were already kept); MUTANT ALIEN opens with SCALE LOCK on (no chromatic notes unless you turn it off).
build 16: ArpEZator 3.2.9 - FL Studio no longer crashes when you close it (the neon face fonts were being freed after FL had already shut its font system down).
